From e8b14ae8cda73c5cacc56681f77be88bb5697dd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CounterStrikeXB2 <cs2@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] nv2a: vertex programs to the back end; answer kickoffs
 mid-walk (CounterStrikeXB2 local patch)

Back end program hand-off. nv2a_backend_register_program() lets a back end
run vertex programs itself (on the GPU). For a program batch that does not
write constants, the executor fetches each distinct vertex index's inputs
once (only the attributes the program reads), builds a triangle list with
odd strip triangles flipped as the hardware assembles them, and passes the
program (start slot..FINAL), c[0..191], the inputs, the fog unit's state and
the usual render state, combiners and stages. A back end that declines gets
the CPU path as before. nv2a_vsh_program() exposes the program and its input
mask; backend_flush's batch-state half is factored out for both paths.

Segment scan answers kickoffs mid-walk. The DMA walk already cleared the PFB
flush bit every 256 words; the default segment scan did not, so a title's
next KickOff spun until the whole segment was executed and the title's CPU
and the executor never overlapped (Counter-Strike: half of every frame).
Bounded so D3D never takes its "GPU far behind" path, whose software-method
interrupt is not delivered: at most 8 kicks per walk and while the title is
under 192 KB past the walked segment, never while a flip is held. The kick
marker latch (PGRAPH 0x400B10, method 0x0310) is now kept for the segment
scan too, since D3D reaches that wait there as well. The method inventory is
collected only when RECOMP_PB_SCAN will report it.
